  "result": "Fixed in `src/click/types.py` (`IntRange._clamp`): the clamp for open bounds moved the value the wrong way, using `bound - dir` instead of `bound + dir`.\n\nFor example, with `IntRange(min=0, min_open=True, clamp=True)`, an input of `-5` clamped to `-1`, which is outside the range, instead of `1`. The same happened for open max bounds, where `max=10, max_open=True` produced `11` instead of `9`.\n\n`tests/test_types.py` passes (41 passed, 2 skipped), though I didn't add a regression test for the open-bound clamp case. `FloatRange` isn't affected, since it raises for clamping with open bounds.",
